; ====================================================================
; comments.cases
; Conformance corpus for the Pasta / Basta COMMENT grammar.
;
; Three comment forms, all of which are `blank` and may appear wherever
; blank may:  ';' line,  '//' line,  '/* */' block.  See ../Basta.txt
; (comment / line-comment / block-comment productions).
;
; Basta shares this production with Pasta exactly; only the blob value differs.
; Comment scanning is never entered inside a blob (blob bytes are consumed by
; length, not scanned as text).
;
; FORMAT / FINGERPRINT are identical to atom-labels.cases; see that file.
; In <input>, \n means a newline and \ a literal backslash.
; ====================================================================

; --- comments: ';' line, '//' line, '/* */' block ----------------------
; All three are `blank` and may appear wherever blank may.  Pasta and Basta
; share this production exactly; only the blob value differs between them.
> {a: 1} ; semi tail
= {a=num}
> ; hdr\n{a: 1}
= {a=num}
> {a: 1} // slash tail
= {a=num}
> // hdr\n{a: 1}
= {a=num}
> {a: 1, // note\n b: 2}
= {a=num,b=num}
> /* hdr */ {a: 1}
= {a=num}
> {a: 1, /* mid */ b: 2}
= {a=num,b=num}
> {a: 1, /* one\ntwo */ b: 2}
= {a=num,b=num}
> ; semi\n// slash\n/* block */\n{a: 1}
= {a=num}
> [1, /* c */ 2, // d\n3]
= [num,num,num]

; --- comment delimiters inside strings are data, not comments ----------
> {a: "http://x/y"}
= {a=str:http://x/y}
> {a: "/* not a comment */"}
= {a=str:/* not a comment */}
> {a: "// not a comment"}
= {a=str:// not a comment}

; --- malformed: unterminated block, bare slash -------------------------
> {a: 1 /* never closed
= ERR
> {a: /}
= ERR
> {a: / 1}
= ERR
